From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qmi_wwan_q: enable QMAPv5 DL checksum offload validation

Mark QMAPv5 downlink packets as CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY when the modem sets
RMNET_MAP_HEADER_TYPE_CSUM_OFFLOAD and csum_valid_required without a
chained next_hdr extension.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/qmi_wwan_q.c
+++ b/qmi_wwan_q.c
@@ -1892,11 +1892,10 @@
 		if(skip_nss)
 			qmap_skb->cb[0] = 1;
 
-		if (ul_header && ul_header->header_type == RMNET_MAP_HEADER_TYPE_CSUM_OFFLOAD
-			&& ul_header->csum_valid_required) {
-#if 0 //TODO
+		if (ul_header &&
+		    ul_header->header_type == RMNET_MAP_HEADER_TYPE_CSUM_OFFLOAD &&
+		    !ul_header->next_hdr && ul_header->csum_valid_required) {
 			qmap_skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY;
-#endif
 		}
 
 		if (qmap_skb->dev->type == ARPHRD_ETHER) {
